{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the day of the week for January 1, 1960, given that January 1, 2000 was a Saturday, we need to calculate the number of days between January 1, 1960 and January 1, 2000 and then determine the day of the week by dividing this number by 7 (since there are 7 days in a week).\n\nFirst, calculate the number of years between 1960 and 2000:\n\\[ 2000 - 1960 = 40 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nNext, determine how many of these years are leap years. A leap year is a year that is divisible by 4, except for end-of-century years, which must be divisible by 400. So, we need to count the leap years in the range from 1960 to 1999.\n\n","prefix_end":620,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,1899,315,279,2003,369,6058,220,16,11,220,16,24,21,15,11,2661,429,6058,220,16,11,220,17,15,15,15,572,264,7728,11,582,1184,311,11047,279,1372,315,2849,1948,6058,220,16,11,220,16,24,21,15,323,6058,220,16,11,220,17,15,15,15,323,1221,8253,279,1899,315,279,2003,553,49702,419,1372,553,220,22,320,11284,1052,525,220,22,2849,304,264,2003,3593,5338,11,11047,279,1372,315,1635,1948,220,16,24,21,15,323,220,17,15,15,15,510,78045,220,17,15,15,15,481,220,16,24,21,15,284,220,19,15,1124,1318,90,1635,92,1124,2533,5847,11,8253,1246,1657,315,1493,1635,525,31471,1635,13,362,31471,1042,374,264,1042,429,374,74916,553,220,19,11,3650,369,835,8668,33357,1635,11,892,1969,387,74916,553,220,19,15,15,13,2055,11,582,1184,311,1760,279,31471,1635,304,279,2088,504,220,16,24,21,15,311,220,16,24,24,24,382,785,31471,1635,304,419,2088,525,25,220,16,24,21,15,11,220,16,24,21,19,11,220,16,24,21,23,11,220,16,24,22,17,11,220,16,24,22,21,11,220,16,24,23,15,11,220,16,24,23,19,11,220,16,24,23,23,11,220,16,24,24,17,11,220,16,24,24,21,13,4504,287,1493,11,582,1490,1052,525,220,16,15,31471,1635,382,54815,11,279,2790,1372,315,2849,1948,6058,220,16,11,220,16,24,21,15,323,6058,220,