e 7 days in a week).\n\nFirst, calculate the number of years between 1960 and 2000:\n\\[ 2000 - 1960 = 40 \\text{ years} \\]\n\nNext, determine how many of these years are leap years. A leap year is a year that is divisible by 4, except for end-of-century years, which must be divisible by 400. So, we need to count the leap years in the range from 1960 to 1999.\n\nThe leap years in this range are: 1960, 1964, 1968, 1972, 1976, 1980, 1984, 1988, 1992, 1996. Counting these, we see there are 10 leap years.\n\nTherefore, the total number of days between January 1, 1960 and January 1, 2000 is:\n\\[ 40 \\text{ years} \\times 365 \\text{ days/year} + 10 \\text{ leap days} = 14600 + 10 = 14610 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find out what day of the week it was 14610 days before January 1, 2000. Since there are 7 days in a week, we divide 14610 by 7 to find the remainder:\n\\[ 14610 \\div 7 = 2087 \\text{ weeks and } 1 \\text{ day remainder} \\]\n\nThis means that January 1, 1960 is 1 day before a Saturday. Since a Saturday minus 1 day is a Friday, January 1, 1960 was a Friday.\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\text{Friday}} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Friday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:44"}
